        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r544681432-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Somber but a must do",
        "text": "This is the sacred cremation site for the Nepali people. They believe that the body needs to be cremated within 24 hours and the ashes pushed into to river in order for their souls to be reincarnated. This was a heartbreaking, somber and private event that is done in such a public way. I stood on the banks of the river crying as the smoke and ash from the fire swirled around me all the while women hawked their jewelry, trash was carelessly tossed in to sacred river and priest charged 100 rubies to have their pictures taken with tourists. But alas this is their way, their customs and their culture. Not worse, not strange or bad. Just different. And I was humbled to be allowed to witness it. ",
