      {
        "review_id": 543931639,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r543931639-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Cultural experience",
        "text": "I've see the reviews that complain about the price and the people and the funerals...ok. Yes, you are not allowed into the temple itself, which is for Hindus only, the only thing that I find negative about this is that I asked my guide how do they know I'm not Hindu, and he said because you're white, which is wrong on so many levels. However, people complained about 1000 rupees price, well book a private tour then. My guide was amazing and explained everything in great detail and it was fascinating. People have also complained about the burning of bodies, why are you in a place of culture of not to appreciate the differences?? The whole ceremony and the traditions behind the funeral and the funeral pyre was very interesting and not disturbing, in fact, the whole process is very beautiful in its own way.  The monkeys are so cute, the whole site is filled with beautiful buildings and get your photo taken with a priest, it costs about 100 rupees, a steal for a great photo (and a blessing).  Well worth the visit with a great guide",
        "review_tip": null,
