        "title": "Religious devotion at its peak. ",
        "text": "A Jyotirling temple connected with Kedarnath darshan and to be done after it.\nThe Pagoda shaped temple building houses many other deities around it and has 4 gates to seek Lord Shiva's blessings from 4 different directions. \nThe cremation pyres outside the main temple near Bahati river is a unique sight and effectively connects the last rites with life and Almighty. \nThe river has been polluted beyond limits turning it into a nulla. Something needs to be done to restore the pious nature of river.\nPlenty of hotels around and the nearby International and Domestic airport make it very easy to visit.",
